      "id": "claim_27d73f87c4c640b1accbb41b63c6b43f",
      "statement": "SSHConnectionWorker and PTY delegate non-PTY exec to the shared owner on existing queues/budgets. PTY runtime commands reuse authenticated transport without hidden authentication, require immediate capacity and a two-second outer deadline, while ordinary control waits with a 15-second deadline. Generation/input validation cancels stale work. Server channel rejection disables runtime control capabilities; configured ceiling one also restricts capabilities, and observation errors publish unavailable state and back off. Ordinary control alone retries pre-exec channel-open failure at 50 ms intervals within its deadline.",
